{#
  Topic filter pills.

  Only renders topics that actually have articles IN THIS LANGUAGE. A pill
  leading to an empty list reads as a broken site, and the three languages
  genuinely differ — Portuguese has fewer articles and fewer topics, and
  swimming currently has none anywhere. Computing this from the posts rather
  than from the vocabulary means the row maintains itself: the pill appears the
  day the first article on that topic publishes, and never before.

  Order follows the vocabulary in i18n.json, not article count, so the row
  doesn't reshuffle every time something publishes.

  No-JS behaviour: these are plain buttons and every card is visible by default.
  Without JS the filter simply does nothing and the full grid still reads fine.
  The buttons are hidden by CSS until JS marks the row ready, so a dead control
  is never shown.
#}
{%- set present = [] -%}
{%- for p in posts -%}
  {%- if p.data.topic and p.data.topic not in present -%}
    {%- set present = (present.push(p.data.topic), present) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if present.length > 1 %}
<div class="topic-filter" data-topic-filter aria-label="{{ t.filterLabel }}">
  <button type="button" class="pill is-active" data-filter="all" aria-pressed="true">{{ t.allTopics }}</button>
  {%- for slug, label in t.topics %}
    {%- if slug in present %}
  <button type="button" class="pill pill--{{ slug }}" data-filter="{{ slug }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ label }}</button>
    {%- endif %}
  {%- endfor %}
</div>
<p class="post-grid__empty" data-no-results hidden>{{ t.noResults }}</p>
<script src="{{ "/assets/js/blog-filter.js" | v }}" defer></script>
{%- endif %}
